# Create repositories from the picker

The picker should offer a fresh-repository candidate above the ordinary plain
candidate. `C-n` creates the selected candidate while retaining the picker.

    :bins jj tmux cat sh sed

> [!NOTE]
> 'jj', 'tmux', 'cat', 'sh', and 'sed' are available.

    :copy tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)
    :w .config/smth/smth.toml (written)

```toml
[repo]
root = "repos"

[tmux]
setup = ": > .smth-ready"
```

    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :t resize-window -t runner:0 -x 120 -y 14 (success)
    :t respawn-pane -k -t runner:0.0 'smth --no-base; cat' (success)
    :pane runner:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)

With an empty query, navigation skips both reserved rows and stays on a live
session.

    :k M-up up up
    :snap

```terminal
session:
  1/1 | [C-r] repo: none | [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
▌⬤ runner                                                                                                              ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────








```

Type a repository name. With no discovered matches, the plain candidate remains
the default even though the fresh-repository candidate appears first.

    :k foo.bar
    :snap

```terminal
session: foo.bar
  0/1 | [C-r] repo: none
   foo-bar                                  ~/r/foo.bar                                                           repo ┃
▌  foo-bar                                                                                                        tmux ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────








```

Select the repository candidate explicitly. Its destination is visible before
creation, and `C-n` creates that exact candidate.

    :k up
    :snap

```terminal
session: foo.bar
  0/1 | [C-r] repo: none
▌  foo-bar                                  ~/r/foo.bar                                                           repo ┃
   foo-bar                                                                                                        tmux ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────








```

    :k C-n
    :$ sh -c 'until test -f repos/foo.bar/.smth-ready; do :; done' (exit: 0)

    :settle -d 2s (settled)

The picker should remain open with its query cleared, and the control-mode
client should remain attached to the runner session.

    :snap

```terminal
session:
  2/2 | [C-r] repo: none | [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
▌⬤ runner                                                                                                              │
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────








```

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}' (success)

```
runner
```

The repository should be colocated, use the configured root, and be attached to
its live tmux session.

    :$ sh -c 'test -d repos/foo.bar/.jj && test -d repos/foo.bar/.git' (exit: 0)

    :$ sh -c 'tmux show-options -qv -t "=foo-bar:" @smth.repo | sed "s#$PWD#<ROOT>#g"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
<ROOT>/repos/foo.bar
```

Occupied paths and invalid directory names should not offer repository candidates.

    :k foo.bar
    :snap "/\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} \d{2}:\d{2}:\d{1,2}/t" "/(?:@|○|◆)\s+([a-z]{8})/w" "/\b([0-9a-f]{8})\b/h"

```terminal
session: foo.bar
  1/2 | [C-r] repo: none | [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
                                                                                                                       ┃
   foo-bar~1                                                                                                      tmux ┃
▌⬤ foo-bar                                  ~/r/foo.bar                                                                ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@  wwwwwwww (no email set) ttttttttttttttttttt hhhhhhhh
│  (empty) (no description set)
◆  wwwwwwww root() hhhhhhhh





```

    :k C-u ../escape
    :snap

```terminal
session: ../escape
  0/2 | [C-r] repo: none
                                                                                                                       ┃
▌  escape                                                                                                         tmux ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────








```

    :k C-u

A query that sanitizes to an empty name should use the first available numeric
session name while preserving the directory name.

    :k ... up
    :snap

```terminal
session: ...
  0/2 | [C-r] repo: none
▌  1                                        ~/r/...                                                               repo ┃
   1                                                                                                              tmux ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────








```

    :k C-n
    :$ sh -c 'until test -f repos/.../.smth-ready; do :; done' (exit: 0)

    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :$ sh -c 'test -d repos/.../.jj && test -d repos/.../.git' (exit: 0)

    :$ sh -c 'tmux show-options -qv -t "=1:" @smth.repo | sed "s#$PWD#<ROOT>#g"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
<ROOT>/repos/...
```

With a repository context, only the workspace candidate is offered. Navigation
must skip the empty row above it, and `C-n` creates the workspace normally.

    :t respawn-pane -k -t runner:0.0 'smth --base repos/foo.bar; cat' (success)
    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :k blocked M-up up up
    :snap "/\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} \d{2}:\d{2}:\d{1,2}/t" "/(?:@|○|◆)\s+([a-z]{8})/w" "/\b([0-9a-f]{8})\b/h"

```terminal
session: blocked
  0/3 | [C-r] repo: ~/r/foo.bar, [C-o] onto: trunk()
                                                                                                                       ┃
▌  foo-bar/blocked                          ~/r/foo.bar.blocked                                              workspace ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@  wwwwwwww (no email set) ttttttttttttttttttt hhhhhhhh
│  (empty) (no description set)
◆  wwwwwwww root() hhhhhhhh





```

    :k C-n
    :$ sh -c 'until test -f repos/foo.bar.blocked/.smth-ready; do :; done' (exit: 0)

    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :snap

```terminal
session:
  4/4 | [C-r] repo: ~/r/foo.bar, [C-o] onto: trunk() | [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
                                                                                                                       ┃
                                                                                                                       ┃
▌⬤ runner                                                                                                              │
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────








```

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}' (success)

```
runner
```

    :$ sh -c 'test -d repos/foo.bar.blocked/.jj && test ! -e repos/blocked' (exit: 0)

    :$ sh -c 'tmux show-options -qv -t "=foo-bar/blocked:" @smth.repo | sed "s#$PWD#<ROOT>#g"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
<ROOT>/repos/foo.bar.blocked
```

